<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#heavy-cavalry">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heavy cavalry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heavy cavalry refers to mounted troops with substantial armour and weapons, used for shock action against enemy formations. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> fielded armoured cavalry as the core of its army, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> faced in its conquests. Mounted warriors were also central to the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry.jpg" alt="Heavy cavalry" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ottoman_Mamluk_horseman_circa_1550.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
